# Coding standards

> Optional seed. Copy to `docs/coding-standards.md` on first need and replace the sample rows below — they are illustrations. While `docs/coding-standards.md` is absent, every command skips its standards step.
> It holds the rules every change must follow: a reviewer may reject a change for one. Traps and notes stay in `.agents/memory/patterns.md`, the "why" in `.agents/memory/decisions.md` — the division: `.agents/memory/reflection-protocol.md` → Standards vs memory.
> Ids `CS-<n>` are stable: never renumbered or reused; a withdrawn rule keeps its heading with `(withdrawn)`. `Enforced by: tool` = a linter, compiler or CI check already fails on it, so reviewers do not re-check it; `Enforced by: review` = a reviewer may reject a change for it and cites the id.
> A convention the code follows in competing ways goes under `## Open — pick one`, never under `## Rules`. Soft limit: 200 lines.

## Rules

### CS-1 — Import another module only through its public entry point
- Enforced by: tool (.eslintrc.json: no-restricted-imports)
- Applies to: `src/**`
- Example: `src/orders/index.ts:1`
- Why: a module's internals can change without breaking its callers.

### CS-2 — Use a helper listed under Shared helpers instead of writing a new one
- Enforced by: review
- Applies to: all code
- Example: `src/lib/http.ts:12`
- Why: copies of one helper drift apart, and each copy needs its own fix.

### CS-3 — Return API errors in the shape named under One shape per problem
- Enforced by: review
- Applies to: `src/api/**`
- Example: `src/api/errors.ts:8`
- Why: callers handle one error body, not several.

## Shared helpers

| Need | Use | Path |
|---|---|---|
| HTTP call with retry and timeout | `httpGet()` | `src/lib/http.ts:12` |

## One shape per problem

| Problem | The shape to use | Reference |
|---|---|---|
| Error response body | `{ "error": { "code", "message" } }` built by `toErrorBody()` | `src/api/errors.ts:8` |

## Open — pick one

- Date handling — native `Date` in `src/orders/`, a date library in `src/billing/`; a person picks one, then it becomes a rule.
